{"term":"retail","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a8e57c56152007534e","definition":"The sale of goods directly to the consumer, encompassing the storefronts, mail-order, websites, etc., and the corporate mechanisms, branding, advertising, etc. that support them.","example":"She works in retail.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["wholesale"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["e-retail","retail apocalypse","retail bank","retail banking","retail credit","retailer","retail park","retail pharmacy","retail politics","retail price","retail theft","retail therapy","e-tail","nonretail","preretail","retailment","retailtainment","wholetail"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c2cc5186112eb40b8b","definition":"The sale of securities or other financial instruments to private investors, as opposed to large institutions.","example":"Mr. Musk reserved a double-digit percentage of the I.P.O. shares for “retail,” or ordinary, investors — as opposed to big institutions.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["wholesale"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["e-retail","retail apocalypse","retail bank","retail banking","retail credit","retailer","retail park","retail pharmacy","retail politics","retail price","retail theft","retail therapy","e-tail","nonretail","preretail","retailment","retailtainment","wholetail"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:39d88492def73b338e","definition":"Retail price; full price; an abbreviated expression, meaning the full suggested price of a particular good or service, before any sale, discount, or other deal.","example":"I never pay retail for clothes.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"a